From e0219dd5c4070c27012c26043682166216301208 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:30:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] SystemUI: Edge light: stop the effect when the pulse
 ends

With the rainbow colour or an animation effect (breathing, wave,
sparkle, chase, comet) selected, an edge light pulse starts animators
that repeat forever next to the one-shot fade that shows the edge.
Only the fade ends on its own, and setPulsing(false) returned before
doing anything, so the rainbow and effect animators kept invalidating
the hidden view on every vsync for as long as the phone stayed dozing.

Stop them and hide the view when the pulse ends, the same way waking
up and unlocking already do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../systemui/edgelight/EdgeLightViewController.kt      | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/edgelight/EdgeLightViewController.kt b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/edgelight/EdgeLightViewController.kt
index 52cdc5fb3a..e6ee08ff3d 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/edgelight/EdgeLightViewController.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/edgelight/EdgeLightViewController.kt
@@ -167,7 +167,15 @@ constructor(
     }
 
     override fun setPulsing(pulsing: Boolean) {
-        if (!currentSettings.isEnabled || !pulsing || !isDozing) return
+        if (!currentSettings.isEnabled) return
+        if (!pulsing) {
+            // The rainbow and effect animators repeat forever; stop them with the pulse, or they
+            // keep invalidating the hidden view for the rest of doze.
+            edgeLightView.pulseRunning = false
+            edgeLightView.visible = false
+            return
+        }
+        if (!isDozing) return
         edgeLightView.apply {
             visible = true
             pulseRunning = true
